## Stable core vs expanding periphery

A two-tier architecture:

- **Stable core** — types that describe the SYSTEM.  Their definitions rarely change; the types themselves are foundational, codify conventions / supertypes / canonical knowledge.  Adding a new stable-core type is a rare architectural event
- **Expanding periphery** — types that describe the WORK.  Their instances accumulate continuously through normal use; mid-conversation captures land here.  Adding a new periphery type is an evolution of the capture vocabulary

Every `type: type` memorial MUST declare a `tier:` field; audit invariant `types-have-tier-classification` enforces at warning severity (warning, not error, because reclassification is a legitimate evolution path).

## Captureability declaration

A type may declare itself captureable mid-conversation via:

- **`mid-conversation-captureable: true`** — type participates in the signal-scan reminder
- **`inject-trigger`** — literal trigger phrases the assistant should watch for
- **`inject-class-name`** — human-readable class name shown in reminders
- **`inject-action`** — what the assistant should DO when the trigger fires
- **`audit-class`** — keyword emitted by audit hooks classifying writes
- **`subtree`** — canonical subtree where instances land

When `mid-conversation-captureable: true`, the partner fields MUST be populated (audit invariant: `captureable-types-have-trigger-and-classname`, error-severity).

